{"version":3,"term":{"cols":80,"rows":24},"timestamp":1790105383,"command":"docker run -t --rm -v /Users/crtah/Data/5-swarm/2-projects/git-swarm:/work --add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway --env-file /var/folders/ky/ms6htv7j6sv5q43hw0gt0bbm0000gn/T/tmp.T5CtqZzfeT git-swarm/harness bash -lc './tests/stack/demo-story.sh'","title":"git-swarm: archive a Radicle repository to Swarm and get it back","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.119, "o", "\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1mgit-swarm — archiving a Radicle repository to Swarm, and getting it back\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2mEvery command below is real. Nothing is mocked or pre-baked.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n"]
[2.009, "o", "\u001b[1mWhat the pieces are\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m  Radicle  peer-to-peer git. No server: a repository lives on whichever\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m           nodes choose to seed it, and its identity, issues and patches\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m           are git objects rather than a database. Its weak spot is that\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m           when nobody seeds a repository any more, it is simply gone.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.011, "o", "\u001b[2m  Swarm    decentralised storage you rent. Content is split into 4 KB\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m           chunks addressed by their hash, and a \"feed\" is a mutable\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m           pointer signed by an Ethereum key — so refs can move, and\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m           anyone can check who moved them. Storage is paid for with a\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m           postage batch, and lapses when the rent stops.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.012, "o", "\u001b[2m  git-swarm  the bridge. git-remote-bzz makes Swarm an ordinary git\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m           remote, so \"git push bzz::…\" works with no server anywhere.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m           Radicle gets durable storage; Swarm gets a real use.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.005, "o", "\r\r\n\u001b[2mRunning against a local five-node bee-factory cluster on a throwaway chain,\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2mnot mainnet Swarm — so nothing here is published to the real network.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2mThe repository is written through one node and read back through a DIFFERENT\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2mone, so \"it worked\" cannot mean \"it was still in the writer's own store\".\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.009, "o", "\r\r\n\u001b[1m── 1. A Radicle repository \u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.321, "o", "   created rad:zNtiZHNnNB9n3j4NK2Rfs4poGnkX\r\r\n\u001b[2m$ cd /rad/demo-origin/storage/zNtiZHNnNB9n3j4NK2Rfs4poGnkX\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.011, "o", "\u001b[2m$ git for-each-ref --format='%(objecttype) %(refname)'\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "commit refs/heads/main\r\r\ncommit refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/cobs/xyz.radicle.id/10d4d29f96…\r\r\ncommit refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/heads/main\r\r\ncommit refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/id\r\r\ncommit refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/root\r\r\ncommit refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/sigrefs\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "commit refs/rad/id\r\r\n"]
[2.010, "o", "\u001b[2m   Under the hood: a Radicle repository on disk is a bare git repo where\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   every peer gets its own refs/namespaces/<node-id>/ subtree. sigrefs is\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   that peer signing its own ref list, so a copy can be checked by anyone\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   without trusting whoever handed it over.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1m── 2. Archive it to Swarm \u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.007, "o", "\u001b[2m   Under the hood: git packs the objects, the helper uploads the pack to\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   Swarm, writes a small JSON manifest listing every ref and pack, and\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   moves a signed feed to point at that manifest. The feed is the only\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   mutable part, and only the key holder can move it.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   A forced refspec, because an archive tracks its source rather than\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   defending a branch from it.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m$ cd /rad/demo-origin/storage/zNtiZHNnNB9n3j4NK2Rfs4poGnkX\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.001, "o", "\u001b[2m$ git push 'bzz::0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266/demo-1790105383' '+refs/*:refs/*' 2>&1 | tail -6\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.826, "o", " * [new reference]   refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/cobs/xyz.radicle.id/10d4d29f96… -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/cobs/xyz.radicle.id/10d4d29f96…\r\r\n * [new reference]   refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/heads/main -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/heads/main\r\r\n * [new reference]   refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/id -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/id\r\r\n * [new reference]   refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/root -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/root\r\r\n * [new reference]   refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/sigrefs -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/sigrefs\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " * [new reference]   refs/rad/id -> refs/rad/id\r\r\n"]
[2.010, "o", "\r\r\n\u001b[1m── 3. Now lose everything \u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.003, "o", "\u001b[2m   Not a simulation: the storage, the identity, the keys, all deleted.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m$ rm -rf /rad/demo-origin\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.010, "o", "\u001b[2m$ ls /rad/demo-origin 2>&1 || echo '   gone.'\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "ls: /rad/demo-origin: No such file or directory\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "   gone.\r\r\n"]
[2.005, "o", "\u001b[2m   On the real network this is every seeder going away. The repository\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   is now unreachable by any Radicle peer.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1m── 4. Restore, holding nothing but a bzz reference \u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.148, "o", "\u001b[2m   A different machine. A different identity. No postage batch and no\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   signing key — reading an archive must never require paying to read it.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   And a different Swarm node: http://host.docker.internal:21635\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   That node never saw the push. If the data had not really propagated,\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   it would have nothing to serve.\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "\u001b[2m$ cd /rad/demo-restored/storage/zNtiZHNnNB9n3j4NK2Rfs4poGnkX\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.011, "o", "\u001b[2m   Propagation is not instant, so this retries until the reader has it.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m$ env -u SWARM_BATCH_ID -u SWARM_PRIVATE_KEY \\\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m    SWARM_API=http://host.docker.internal:21635 SWARM_GATEWAY=http://host.docker.internal:21635 \\\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m    git fetch 'bzz::0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266/demo-1790105383' '+refs/*:refs/*'\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[1.217, "o", "swarm: downloading pack 1/1 (2271 bytes)\r\r\nFrom bzz::0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266/demo-1790105383\r\r\n * [new branch]      main        -> main\r\r\n * [new ref]         refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/cobs/xyz.radicle.id/10d4d29f96… -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/cobs/xyz.radicle.id/10d4d29f96…\r\r\n * [new ref]         refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/heads/main -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/heads/main\r\r\n * [new ref]         refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/id -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/id\r\r\n * [new ref]         refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/root -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/root\r\r\n * [new ref]         refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/sigrefs -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/sigrefs\r\r\n * [new ref]         refs/rad/id -> refs/rad/id\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m   arrived after 1 attempt(s)\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1m── 5. Is it really the same repository? \u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.004, "o", "\u001b[2m$ git for-each-ref --format='%(objecttype) %(refname)'\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "commit refs/heads/main\r\r\ncommit refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/cobs/xyz.radicle.id/10d4d29f96…\r\r\ncommit refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/heads/main\r\r\ncommit refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/id\r\r\ncommit refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/root\r\r\ncommit refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/sigrefs\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "commit refs/rad/id\r\r\n"]
[2.007, "o", "\u001b[2m$ git fsck --no-progress --no-dangling && echo '   fsck: clean'\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.006, "o", "notice: HEAD points to an unborn branch (master)\r\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "   fsck: clean\r\r\n"]
[2.013, "o", "\u001b[2m   And Radicle itself accepts it — identity and delegates recovered\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   from the archive, by an identity that has never seen this repo:\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m$ RAD_HOME=/rad/demo-restored rad inspect --identity rad:zNtiZHNnNB9n3j4NK2Rfs4poGnkX | head -14\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "{\r\r\n  \"payload\": {\r\r\n    \"xyz.radicle.project\": {\r\r\n      \"defaultBranch\": \"main\",\r\r\n      \"description\": \"git-swarm archive fixture\",\r\r\n      \"name\": \"fixture\"\r\r\n    }\r\r\n  },\r\r\n  \"delegates\": [\r\r\n    \"did:key:z6Mkt9GSjU3is39DSpzbRBcEAiyBS5ism4Gbmd9tX372aG7e\"\r\r\n  ],\r\r\n  \"threshold\": 1\r\r\n}\r\r\n"]
[2.005, "o", "\r\r\n\u001b[1m── 6. Put it back on the network \u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.002, "o", "\u001b[2m$ RAD_HOME=/rad/demo-restored rad seed rad:zNtiZHNnNB9n3j4NK2Rfs4poGnkX 2>&1 | tail -1\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "✓ Seeding policy updated for rad:zNtiZHNnNB9n3j4NK2Rfs4poGnkX with scope 'followed'\r\r\n"]
[3.018, "o", "\u001b[2m   node started\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\u001b[2m$ RAD_HOME=/rad/demo-restored rad node inventory\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "\u001b[36mrad:zNtiZHNnNB9n3j4NK2Rfs4poGnkX\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.007, "o", "\u001b[2m   Inventory is what a node announces it will serve. The repository is\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   back on the network, from an archive, after every peer was gone.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   Under the hood: restoring took two things — the git objects, and a\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   seeding policy telling the node it should carry this repository.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1m── 7. And it is readable with no Radicle at all \u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.019, "o", "\u001b[2m   A PATH with git, node and the helper — and nothing from Radicle:\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m$ PATH=/tmp/demo-bin command -v rad || echo '   rad: not found'\u001b[0m\r\r\n   rad: not found\r\r\n"]
[2.015, "o", "\u001b[2m$ cd /tmp/demo-plain.git\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[2.002, "o", "\u001b[2m$ PATH=/tmp/demo-bin env -u SWARM_BATCH_ID -u SWARM_PRIVATE_KEY SWARM_API=http://host.docker.internal:21635 SWARM_GATEWAY=http://host.docker.internal:21635 git fetch 'bzz::0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266/demo-1790105383' '+refs/*:refs/*' 2>&1 | tail -3\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[1.228, "o", " * [new ref]         refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/root -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/root\r\r\n * [new ref]         refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/sigrefs -> refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/rad/sigrefs\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " * [new ref]         refs/rad/id -> refs/rad/id\r\r\n"]
[2.003, "o", "\u001b[2m$ PATH=/tmp/demo-bin git for-each-ref --count=3 --format='%(refname)'\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "refs/heads/main\r\r\nrefs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/cobs/xyz.radicle.id/10d4d29f96…\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "refs/namespaces/z6Mkt9GSjU3i…/refs/heads/main\r\r\n"]
[2.004, "o", "\r\r\n\u001b[1m── Done \u001b[0m\r\r\n   Archived to Swarm, lost completely, restored through a node that\r\r\n   never saw the push, re-seeded onto the network, and readable with\r\r\n   stock git alone.\r\r\n\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m   Local bee-factory cluster, not mainnet. Write node http://host.docker.internal:21633,\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[2m   read node http://host.docker.internal:21635.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n   Clone it with the helper:\r\r\n     git clone bzz::0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266/demo-1790105383\r\r\n\r\r\n   Or browse it: the push above printed a feed manifest reference.\r\r\n   Open the viewer against this cluster with\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     ?gateway=$SWARM_GATEWAY#bzz/<that reference>\r\r\n\r\r\n"]
[0.188, "x", "0"]
